ProjectALife.DialogueShards["radio_2"] = {
{"king_radio_not_certain","host",1,3650,0,23,1,{"June","I've been thinking about how often I used to say definitely","June","Definitely tomorrow. Definitely all right","June","Sometimes I meant I hope so","June","Those aren't the same thing","June","If I sound less sure lately, I'm trying to be honest","June","Not to frighten you","June","You deserve to know which things I actually know","June","I'll keep working on the difference"}},
{"r1_d1_swat_6068_louisville_road","scanner",1,1,6,14,3,{"Louisville Radio","6-Robert-23, 6-Robert-21, SWAT callout, barricaded subject with hostages, 6068 Louisville Road","6-Robert-23","6-Robert-23 en route to 6068 Louisville Road, Code 3, with the van","Louisville Radio","Robert-23, patrol on scene reports one male subject holding three family members in the basement - he won't pick up the phone for the negotiator","6-Robert-23","Copy - any weapons?","Louisville Radio","Unknown, patrol reports screaming from the basement windows - no demands","6-Robert-23","Team's on scene, setting the inner perimeter - negotiator is on the bullhorn now","6-Robert-23","Radio, the negotiator's been on the bullhorn five minutes, the subject is moving toward the noise, not away from it - the family is yelling for us to come in","6-Robert-23","We're making entry - hold the air","Louisville Radio","All units, hold your traffic for SWAT","6-Robert-21","Shots fired, shots fired! Subject down! Subject is back up!","6-Robert-23","Put him down! Radio, the subject took four rounds to the chest and kept walking - the last one was a head shot, subject is down","6-Robert-23","Three family members out, two with bite injuries - send EMS to the front, and tell them gloves and eye protection","Louisville Radio","EMS advises they will not enter the scene, they'll take patients at the curb","6-Robert-23","Then we'll carry them to the curb. 6-Robert-23, scene is secure"}},
{"r1_d1_air1_dixie_siren_crowd","scanner",1,1,12,19,2,{"Air-1","Air-1 to all Southwest units, Dixie Highway corridor","Air-1","I have a large group on foot southbound on Dixie at Greenwood Road - I'd estimate two hundred, they're in all four lanes","Louisville Radio","Air-1, is this a civil disturbance?","Air-1","Negative, no signs, no shouting, they're walking behind 2-Adam-14's car, it's the siren, they're following the siren","2-Adam-14","2-Adam-14, siren's off, I'm trying to get around them","Air-1","Adam-14, the front of that group is thirty yards off your bumper - do not stop","Air-1","All units in Southwest, run dark - no sirens, every siren in this district is dragging a crowd behind it","Louisville Radio","All Southwest units, Air-1 advises lights only, no sirens, until further notice","Air-1","They're starting to look up at me now, I'm moving off east to see if they follow the rotor","Air-1","Confirmed, half the group is turning east after the aircraft - I'm going to drag them as far as my fuel allows"}},
{"r1_d1_boil_water_scanner_press","scanner",1,1,6,13,1,{"Knox 11","Knox 11 to Knox 4 - Donna got the TV on at the house?","Knox 4","She says Channel 11 is running a boil water advisory for the county - that's it, that's all the news there is","Knox 11","Boil water, I just spent an hour at the trailer park on Rock Haven Road with a man chewing through a screen door","Knox 4","Maybe he should have boiled his water","Knox 20","Knox 20 to both of you - get off the air with that, every reporter in Louisville has a scanner tuned to this channel","Knox 11","Copy, Sarge - Knox 11 has nothing to report but the weather","Knox 20","Good, keep it that way - find a landline for anything else"}},
{"r1_d1_hospital_bay_locked","scanner",1,1,5,12,1,{"Knox 15","Knox 15 to dispatch, I'm at the hospital emergency entrance","Knox 15","The administrator is asking me to lock the ambulance bay doors - Medic 2's crew is still outside unloading","Dispatch","Knox 15, can you get the crew in first?","Knox 15","Their patient is fighting the straps on the cot, the nurses won't take him through the door","Medic 2","Medic 2 to Knox 15 - lock it, we'll put him back in the rig","Knox 15","Medic 2, you sure?","Medic 2","We're sure - tell them we're going back to quarters, and tell them we want our blankets back","Knox 15","Doors are locked, dispatch, the hospital is closed to ambulances as of now - walk-ins only, through the front, and they're screening at the door","Dispatch","Screening for what, Knox 15?","Knox 15","Arms and legs, anybody with a bite waits outside under the awning"}},
{"r1_d1_rosewood_drunk_tank","scanner",1,1,6,12,1,{"Rosewood Jail","Rosewood Jail to any Rosewood unit, I need a hand in the back","Rosewood 5","Rosewood 5, go ahead","Rosewood Jail","The drunk tank, fella we brought in last night quit breathing on me around six - I called for EMS - EMS never came","Rosewood Jail","Now he's up, his cellmate is standing on the bench hollering for me to open the door","Rosewood 5","Don't open that door by yourself, Arliss, I'm five minutes out","Rosewood Jail","I'm not opening anything, the cellmate's talking to me through the food slot, he wants to know if he can have his phone call now","Rosewood 5","Tell him yes, tell him he can call anybody in the world when I get there","Rosewood Jail","Rosewood 5, step on it, he's climbing the bars"}},
{"r1_d1_dixie_village_balconies","scanner",1,1,10,20,2,{"Dispatch","Muldraugh Fire, Engine 21, Truck 23, Tanker 41, working fire, Dixie Village apartments, building C. Multiple callers with people trapped upstairs","Truck 23","Truck 23 on scene, three-story, fire on the first floor, east end - occupants out on the second and third floor balconies waving","Engine 21","Engine 21, I'll be Dixie Command - truck 23, can you reach the balconies?","Truck 23","Affirmative, Command, but the occupants are yelling for us not to use the stairwell - they say the stairwell's full","Dixie Command","Full of fire?","Truck 23","Negative, full of people - people who aren't right, I can see them through the stairwell windows","Dixie Command","Nobody enters that stairwell, truck 23, ladder evacuation off the balconies - engine 21, put a line on the fire and keep it off the stairs","Truck 23","First family coming down, mother, two kids, and a cat in a laundry basket","Dixie Command","Get the cat too","Truck 23","Already down, the cat's in better shape than we are","Tanker 41","Tanker 41 on scene, the hydrant on the corner is barely giving us anything - everybody in Muldraugh's got a garden hose running","Dixie Command","Copy, 41, set up a shuttle - we'll be here a while"}},
{"r1_d1_post4_turn_them_back","scanner",1,1,0,9,1,{"Post 4","Post 4 to all Post 4 units, by order of the Commander, set up traffic control on US-31W at the Hardin County line and on US-60 at Irvington","Post 4","All traffic leaving Knox County is to be turned back - no exceptions without a supervisor present","Trooper 410","410 copies, post, the first thing these folks are going to ask me is why","Post 4","410, tell them the road is closed by the Kentucky State Police","Trooper 410","And when they ask me why it's closed?","Post 4","Same answer, 410","Trooper 410","10-4, I've got a line of cars back to the overpass already - there's a station wagon with a grandmother riding in a lawn chair in the back","Post 4","Turn them around, 410","Trooper 410","Turning them around, grandma waved at me"}},
{"r1_d1_hardin12_crosses_over","scanner",1,1,8,16,2,{"Hardin 12","Hardin 12 to Knox County Dispatch, I'm crossing into your county on mutual aid - what channel do you want me on?","Dispatch","Hardin 12, stay right here - go to West Point High School, the gym's being set up for a shelter and they need a car","Hardin 12","Copy, heads up, dispatch, I passed the state police at the line - they let me in, but they're turning back everything with Knox County plates","Dispatch","We heard - Hardin 12, what's your name?","Hardin 12","Deputy Russ Keene - why?","Dispatch","Because you're the only help anybody's sent me today, and I'd like to be able to thank you by name","Hardin 12","Save the thanks till I've done something, show me en route"}},
{"r1_d1_missy_yellow_dog","scanner",1,1,9,19,2,{"Dispatch","Knox 9, Knox 12, missing juvenile, March Ridge, 3000 block of Oak Ridge Court - female, six years old, answers to Missy, pink shorts, no shoes","Knox 9","Knox 9 en route - how long has she been gone?","Dispatch","The mother says about forty minutes, there was trouble at the neighbor's and the girl ran out the back door","Knox 12","Knox 12, I've got Bo with me - he'll track a kid","Knox 12","Track started at the back step, he's pulling hard","Knox 9","Knox 9, there's two of those sick ones in the street out front - I'll keep them looking at me","Knox 12","Knox 12 - Bo's stopped at a doghouse three yards over, his tail's going","Knox 12","Found her, she's inside the doghouse with a big yellow dog, the dog's got his head across her lap and he won't let me near","Dispatch","Is she hurt?","Knox 12","Not a scratch, she says the dog told her to be quiet, I'm not arguing with either one of them","Knox 12","Tell her mother we've got her, and whoever owns this yellow dog, he's getting a steak if I ever find one"}},
{"r1_d1_fellowship_hall_reception","scanner",1,1,13,21,1,{"Dispatch","Knox 11, disturbance at the fellowship hall behind Hill Grove Baptist, Brandenburg Road - a wedding reception","Knox 11","Knox 11 en route - somebody spike the punch?","Dispatch","Negative, caller is the father of the bride - he says a guest collapsed on the dance floor, and when he came to, he bit the bride's mother","Knox 11","Knox 11, 10-23, the guests are all out in the parking lot, they've got the hall doors shut and three groomsmen leaning on them","Knox 11","The one who collapsed is inside with two others, the groom says one of them is his uncle","Dispatch","Knox 11, do you need EMS?","Knox 11","For the mother of the bride, she's sitting on a tailgate in her good dress with a napkin on her wrist, telling everybody to go ahead and cut the cake","Knox 11","Dispatch, the bride wants to know if she's still married, since the preacher never signed the license","Dispatch","Tell her that's above my pay grade, tell her congratulations"}},
{"r1_d1_double_1033_cedar_otter","scanner",1,1,20,3,2,{"Knox 15","Dispatch, Knox 15! 10-33! I'm at Cedar and (stepped on)","Dispatch","Unit calling 10-33, you're unreadable, two units keyed at once, all units, clear the channel - emergency traffic only","Knox 15","Knox 15! Cedar Lane at the water tower! I've got a family behind me and they're coming across the yard!","Knox 9","Knox 9! 10-33, Otter Creek bridge!","Dispatch","Knox 15, copy Cedar Lane at the water tower - Knox 9, copy Otter Creek bridge - any unit to back either one?","Hardin 12","Hardin 12, I'm a mile from Cedar - going","Dispatch","Knox 9, status?","Dispatch","Knox 9, Knox County - status","Knox 9","Knox 9 - I'm okay, I drove through them - I'm okay, my windshield's gone","Hardin 12","Hardin 12 on Cedar, I've got half the family in my back seat and Knox 15's got the other half - we're leaving","Knox 15","Knox 15 is okay - Knox 15 is okay - tell Hardin 12 he's got a friend in this county for life"}},
{"r1_d1_trooper435_minivan","scanner",1,1,10,20,1,{"Trooper 435","Post 4, 435, a vehicle just ran my traffic point on US-60, westbound out of Irvington - blue minivan","Post 4","435, are you in pursuit?","Trooper 435","Affirmative, speeds about seventy, I can see three child seats through the back glass","Post 4","Sergeant advises at your discretion, 435","Trooper 435","I'm backing off, I'm not putting a car full of kids in a ditch over a roadblock","Post 4","Copy, 435 terminating","Trooper 435","Post, let Breckinridge County know they've got a blue minivan coming - tell them the father's just trying to get his kids someplace","Post 4","Breckinridge is closing its line too, 435, he won't get far","Trooper 435","Then I hope he finds a motel with a pool"}},
{"r1_d1_boy22_sporting_goods_line","scanner",1,1,9,17,1,{"Louisville Radio","4-Boy-22, crowd control request at the sporting goods store on Dixie Highway - manager reports a fight in the line out front","4-Boy-22","4-Boy-22, 10-23, the line goes around the building and down past the tire place - three hundred people, easy","4-Boy-22","The manager's selling through the drive-up window he rigged in the stockroom door - cash only, two boxes of shells per customer","Louisville Radio","What was the fight about, Boy-22?","4-Boy-22","Man in line coughing, people thought he was sick - he says it's hay fever, he's got the tissues to prove it","4-Boy-22","I'm standing next to him now so folks settle down - radio, the manager says the shotguns are gone and he's on to the pellet rifles","Louisville Radio","Copy - stay with the line till it clears","4-Boy-22","There's a lady in line buying a slingshot and a bag of marbles - I'm not going to say a word to her"}},
{"r1_d1_callback_offduty_roll","scanner",1,1,7,15,1,{"Louisville Radio","All cars, all districts, the Chief has cancelled all days off and vacations, all off-duty personnel report to their districts immediately","2-Adam-31","2-Adam-31, Radio, I'm reporting in my own truck, I've got my badge clipped to my T-shirt and my service weapon - that's the uniform today","Louisville Radio","Copy, Adam-31, report to Second District","3-Charles-8","3-Charles-8, I was on the lake in Indiana - the bridge is shut from their side, so I rowed over - I'll need a ride from the river","Louisville Radio","3-Charles-8, say again, you rowed across the Ohio?","3-Charles-8","Borrowed a johnboat, I'll bring it back to the man when this is over - put that in the log so he knows","4-Boy-40","4-Boy-40, I was coaching my daughter's softball tournament, I've got eleven twelve-year-olds in my station wagon - where do you want them?","Louisville Radio","Take them to Fourth District, somebody will sort out parents","4-Boy-40","Copy, they want to know if they won by forfeit"}},
{"r1_d1_trooper422_tire_iron_note","scanner",1,1,7,15,2,{"Trooper 422","Post 4, 422, I'm back at the I-65 southbound rest area, the charter bus from last night","Post 4","Go ahead, 422","Trooper 422","It's empty, the door's been pried open from outside with a tire iron - the tire iron's lying on the pavement next to it","Trooper 422","Somebody let them out, Post","Post 4","Any idea who?","Trooper 422","There's a pickup by the vending machines with Tennessee plates and a note on the dash - it says, I came for my wife","Post 4","Copy, 422 - any sign of the owner?","Trooper 422","No sign of anybody, I'm leaving the note where it is - show me clear"}},
{"r1_d1_ems1_four_points","scanner",1,1,6,18,1,{"EMS 1","EMS 1 to all county ambulances","EMS 1","Effective immediately, no crew member rides in the back with a bite patient unless that patient is fully restrained - four points, and a mask on the face","Medic 3","Medic 3 - EMS 1, that's going to cause problems with airway management","EMS 1","I know what it does to airway management, Medic 3 - your partner is home with a fever - follow the order","Medic 3","Medic 3 copies","EMS 1","Second, if a patient arrests en route, you pull over, you get out, you shut the doors, and you call it in","Medic 2","Medic 2 - EMS 1, and then what?","EMS 1","Then you wait for law enforcement, you do not work the code - I'm sorry, everybody, that's all I've got"}},
{"r1_d1_muldraugh3_partner_down","scanner",1,1,14,23,2,{"Muldraugh 3","Muldraugh 3, officer down! Main and Dixie! My partner's bit!","Dispatch","10-33, all units, officer down, Main Street at 31W - Muldraugh 3, how bad?","Muldraugh 3","His neck - it's bad, I got the subject, he's down - send me EMS!","Dispatch","Medic 2 is en route, eight minutes - keep pressure on it","Muldraugh 3","I'm holding it, I'm holding it","Dispatch","Muldraugh 3, you've got an open mic - keep holding pressure","Knox 11","Knox 11, two minutes out","Knox 11","Knox 11 on scene, dispatch, have Medic 2 slow down - no lights","Dispatch","Copy - Medic 2, slow it down","Knox 11","Dispatch, give Muldraugh 3 a minute, he'll be back on the air when he can"}},
{"r1_d1_sarge_policy_mr_phelps","scanner",1,1,17,23,1,{"Knox 20","Knox 20 to all units, the Sheriff asked me to put this out over the air, so here it is","Knox 20","The deadly force policy has not changed, if a subject is attacking you or a citizen and you believe it means death or serious injury, you know what you're authorized to do","Knox 20","What we're hearing from Louisville is it has to be the head - I don't like saying that on the air either","Knox 4","Knox 4 - Sarge, the one I had this afternoon was Mr. Phelps - he sold me my first truck","Knox 20","I know, Knox 4","Knox 4","Does the policy cover Mr. Phelps?","Knox 20","It covers what came at you - not him - write it that way in your report, and then go home and see your wife"}},
{"r1_d1_medic3_rent_rock_haven","scanner",1,1,11,22,1,{"Medic 3","Medic 3, dispatch, we're 10-33, we're locked in the back of the box at 1100 Rock Haven Road","Dispatch","Medic 3, what's your situation?","Medic 3","The patient's family turned on us when we walked in - we made it to the unit, they're rocking it","Dispatch","Nearest unit is Hardin 12, about twelve minutes - lock the side door - stay in the back","Medic 3","Side door's locked, rear doors are locked - my EMT's holding the handle anyway","Dispatch","Stay off the windows, check in with me every two minutes","Medic 3","Medic 3, still here, they're on the hood - I can hear one on the roof","Dispatch","Two minutes, Medic 3 - still with me?","Medic 3","Still here, my EMT says tell you we're going to start charging them rent","Hardin 12","Hardin 12, turning onto Rock Haven Road with my lights on - Medic 3, when they come to me, you drive","Medic 3","They're coming off the hood, they're going to your lights - we're rolling"}},
{"r1_d1_tanker41_paddock_fence","scanner",1,1,14,22,1,{"Tanker 41","Tanker 41 on scene at the barn fire on Bethel Church Road - the barn's fully involved - we're defensive","Tanker 41","Dispatch, the owner's asking us to cut her paddock fence and turn the horses loose","Dispatch","Is there a reason she can't open the gate?","Tanker 41","The gate's on the far side, and there's four or five people standing around it - they're not firemen and they're not neighbors","Tanker 41","Cutting the fence on our side, the horses are out, headed for the tree line at a dead run","Tanker 41","The owner's counting them, she's got six, she says there ought to be seven","Dispatch","Copy, Tanker 41","Tanker 41","She's standing by the cut in the fence with a bucket of feed, shaking it - we're going to let her"}},
{"r1_d1_coroner_closed_sign","scanner",1,1,10,20,1,{"Coroner","Coroner to Knox County","Dispatch","Go ahead, coroner","Coroner","Advise all units I have no more room, the funeral homes in Muldraugh and West Point are full, and the hospital morgue is locked","Coroner","Units with a deceased at a scene, cover the remains, note the address and the time, and leave them - I'll come when I can","Knox 9","Knox 9, coroner, I've got one at the laundromat on Main, I can't leave him in the dryer room with people walking in","Coroner","Then lock the laundromat, Knox 9, tape a note to the door","Knox 9","What do I write on it?","Coroner","Closed, just write closed"}},
{"r1_d1_knox7_porch_light","scanner",1,1,6,12,2,{"Dispatch","Knox 7, Knox County","Dispatch","Knox 7, Knox County, radio check","Knox 20","Knox 20 - dispatch, has anybody heard from Knox 7 since he went home last night?","Dispatch","Negative, his home phone rings and rings","Knox 20","I'll swing by. 400 block of Walnut","Knox 20","Knox 20, 10-23 at Knox 7's residence, his cruiser's in the driveway - porch light's still on","Knox 20","Door's locked, I can hear him moving around inside","Dispatch","Is he answering you, Knox 20?","Knox 20","No, show me back in service - I'm leaving him be for now - show Knox 7 out of service","Dispatch","Knox 7 out of service at {time}"}},
{"r1_d1_crackers_code_two","scanner",1,1,16,23,1,{"Dispatch","All Knox units, be advised day shift dispatch did not report in - I'll stay on the console until relief","Knox 11","Linda, you've been on since three yesterday","Dispatch","Keep it off the air, Knox 11","Knox 9","Knox 9, somebody bring that woman a sandwich","Knox 12","Knox 12, I've got a pack of peanut butter crackers and a warm cola - I'll bring it by","Dispatch","The back door stays locked, slide it through the records window","Knox 12","10-4, crackers are en route, Code 3","Knox 20","Nobody runs Code 3 for crackers","Knox 12","Code 2 for crackers, Sarge"}},
{"r1_d1_knox11_quiet_prisoner","scanner",1,1,0,5,1,{"Knox 11","Knox 11 to the county jail, I'm ten minutes out with one in custody - assault on a family member","County Jail","Jail copies - how's he acting?","Knox 11","He was cussing me the whole way from Brandenburg, about five minutes ago he quit","Knox 11","Now he's got his face pressed up against the cage, right behind my head - breathing on the glass - no talking","County Jail","Is he breathing, Knox 11, or is that you guessing?","Knox 11","Somebody's fogging up that glass, I'm not pulling over to check which one of us it is","County Jail","Knox 11, jail commander says we're not accepting anyone with a fever or a bite - is he bitten?","Knox 11","His mother bit him, that's the assault, she's the victim - I was going to let you sort that out","County Jail","Negative on intake - take him somewhere else","Knox 11","There is nowhere else, I'm going to park in the sally port and sit here till somebody tells me something"}},
{"r1_d1_news_van_cameraman","scanner",1,1,12,20,1,{"6-Robert-21","6-Robert-21 to Radio, there's a TV news van parked inside our outer perimeter on Louisville Road - Cameraman's walking up the driveway","Louisville Radio","Robert-21, have patrol move them back to the tape","6-Robert-21","Patrol is busy, I'm doing it - Sir, back to the tape - Sir, there's one coming out of the side yard, get back to the van","6-Robert-21","He's filming it, he's still filming it, he's down, he's got him by the leg!","6-Robert-23","Robert-23 moving to you","6-Robert-21","Subject is down, cameraman has a bite on his calf, the reporter's in the van with the doors locked, screaming at me to give her the tape","Louisville Radio","Robert-21, the camera is evidence - secure it","6-Robert-21","The camera's secured, the cameraman wants to know if he gets overtime for this - I told him to sit down and hold his leg up"}},
{"r2_d1_frago_trace","military",1,1,5,11,2,{"Warden Main","All Warden stations, Warden Main - Fragmentary order follows, prepare to copy, over","Hatchet-6","Hatchet-6, ready to copy, over","Warden Main","Traffic control points go in by 1200 today - TCP 1, the Louisville bridge approach - TCP 2, Dixie Highway north of West Point - break","Warden Main","TCP 3, Highway 60 at the county line - TCP 4, the Brandenburg road - TCP 5 and TCP 6, the county roads south of Rosewood - break","Warden Main","Mission at every point, no persons, vehicles, animals or cargo leave the county - read back the mission only, over","Hatchet-6","Hatchet-6 reads back, no persons, vehicles, animals or cargo leave the county, over","Warden Main","Read back correct, inbound traffic is stopped as well, anyone inside stays inside, over","Hatchet-6","Roger, request guidance on residents stuck outside who are trying to get home from work, over","Warden Main","They do not get home - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r2_d1_rules_readback","military",1,2,0,23,1,{"Warden-3","All Warden stations, Warden-3, change to the rules of engagement, effective immediately - Commanders acknowledge and read back, over","Warden-3","One, challenge any person approaching a checkpoint by voice and loudspeaker at the greatest range you can be heard","Warden-3","Two, a person who continues past the final warning point may be stopped with deadly force - three, warning shots at the commander's discretion - over","Hatchet-6","Hatchet-6, request clarification on item two - does that include persons showing no sign of illness, over?","Warden-3","Item two makes no distinction - read back, over","Hatchet-6","Hatchet-6 reads back, voice and loudspeaker at greatest range, deadly force past the final warning point, no distinction - warning shots at my discretion, over","Warden-3","Correct, you will brief every soldier on the line personally before dark, over","Hatchet-6","Roger - Sir, some of my soldiers live in Muldraugh, over","Warden-3","Understood, brief them anyway - Warden-3, out"}},
{"r2_d1_church_van_water","military",1,2,9,19,1,{"Crowbar-2-6","Crowbar-6, Crowbar-2-6 at TCP 5, white church van, fourteen residents from a nursing home in Rosewood - the driver has a letter from the facility, over","Crowbar-6","Does the letter change the order, over?","Crowbar-2-6","Negative, but two of them are on oxygen and the bottles are low - the driver says he was told to take them to a hospital in Bowling Green, over","Crowbar-6","Nobody on this end authorized that - is anyone aboard sick, over?","Crowbar-2-6","Old and hot is all I can see from here - one lady keeps tapping on the window and waving at my gunner, over","Crowbar-6","Wait one","Crowbar-6","Crowbar-2-6, battalion says negative, the van goes back to Rosewood, over","Crowbar-2-6","Roger - Sir, can I at least give them the water cans off my truck, over?","Crowbar-6","Set the cans on the road and back your people off fifty meters before the driver picks them up - out"}},
{"r2_d1_scout_median","military",1,2,6,19,1,{"Bluejay 2-4","Warden Main, Bluejay 2-4 - spot report - Dixie Highway southbound is jammed solid from Muldraugh to the Fort Knox gate, over","Warden Main","Bluejay 2-4, send it, over","Bluejay 2-4","Vehicles stopped, a lot of them abandoned with the doors open - several hundred people on foot walking between the cars toward the gate, over","Warden Main","Any movement against that traffic, over?","Bluejay 2-4","Affirmative, small groups walking north up the median, slow, straight into the crowd - the crowd is scattering wherever they meet, over","Warden Main","Say again, scattering, over?","Bluejay 2-4","Scattering, people climbing up on car roofs - I'm at five hundred feet and I can hear the horns through my headset, over","Warden Main","Bluejay 2-4, maintain altitude, do not descend for any reason - continue north and report on the bridge, over","Bluejay 2-4","Wilco - Continuing north to the bridge - Bluejay 2-4, out"}},
{"r2_d1_packhorse_sp","military",1,1,12,17,1,{"Packhorse-5","Warden Main, Packhorse-5, crossing the start point at 1410 with nine vehicles, water, rations, medical supply and body bags for the holding areas, over","Warden Main","Packhorse-5, roger SP at 1410, route is Dixie Highway north to Muldraugh, then the county road to Riverside - call each checkpoint as you pass, over","Packhorse-5","Roger - be advised, vehicle seven has a bad fuel pump, if it quits, I cross-load and leave it, over","Warden Main","Approved, do not stop for civilians on the route for any reason - acknowledge, over","Packhorse-5","Acknowledged - what do I do if they block the road, over?","Warden Main","Lay on the horn and keep rolling at a walking pace - they'll move, over","Packhorse-5","And if they don't move, over?","Warden Main","Then you call me and I'll find you an answer - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r2_d1_guard_old_sets","military",1,3,0,23,1,{"Thoroughbred 2-6","Any Army station this net, Thoroughbred 2-6, Kentucky National Guard, on the Brandenburg road - how copy, over?","Hatchet-6","Thoroughbred 2-6, Hatchet-6, weak and broken - why are you transmitting single channel in the clear, over?","Thoroughbred 2-6","Because that's what our sets do, we never got the new radios, somebody promised us them in 1991, over","Hatchet-6","Then you can't join my net, every word you say is going out to every scanner in the county, over","Thoroughbred 2-6","I'll take my chances, I have forty men, three trucks and no orders past get to Brandenburg - who do I work for, over?","Hatchet-6","Wait one","Hatchet-6","Thoroughbred 2-6, as of now you work for me - hold the Brandenburg road until relieved, send a runner to TCP 3 for a radio that can talk to mine, over","Thoroughbred 2-6","Roger, a runner, like it's the Civil War - Thoroughbred 2-6, out"}},
{"r2_d1_categories_defined","military",1,3,0,23,1,{"Warden Main","All Warden stations, Warden Main, new brevity terms effective now - stand by to copy, over","Warden Main","Category One, a civilian with no symptoms - Category Two, a civilian bitten, scratched or running a fever - Category Three, a person who has died and is still moving - over","Hatchet-6","Hatchet-6 copies One, Two and Three - guidance on a Category Two who says he cut his arm on a fence, over?","Warden Main","A cut is a cut, he's a Two, over","Crowbar-6","Crowbar-6 - Warden Main, how long does a Two stay a Two, over?","Warden Main","Unknown, medical says hours, some less - treat every Two as a Three that hasn't happened yet, over","Crowbar-6","Roger - Crowbar-6, out"}},
{"r2_d1_trooper_relay","military",1,3,0,23,1,{"Trooper Haskins","Army net, this is a Kentucky State Police trooper on a borrowed radio at TCP 3 - I need a relay to Frankfort, over","Warden Main","Station calling, you are on a military net, state your traffic, over","Trooper Haskins","My post's tower went down Friday night and dispatch won't answer - I have eleven troopers unaccounted for inside your line - Frankfort needs to know that, over","Warden Main","We have no link to Frankfort, I can pass it to our higher, over","Trooper Haskins","Pass it, then, and tell them I didn't abandon my cruiser, it's parked across the on-ramp at West Point on purpose, over","Warden Main","Roger, eleven troopers unaccounted for - your name, over?","Trooper Haskins","Trooper Dale Haskins, they'll know the name at the post - they would have, anyway, over","Warden Main","Copy, Trooper Haskins, I need this net clear now - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r2_d1_berm_cows","military",1,3,7,20,1,{"Sapper-6","Warden Main, Sapper-6, berm complete on the Fallas Lake road, twelve feet of fill, eighty meters wide, over","Warden Main","Roger - any civilian resistance, over?","Sapper-6","Farmer drove out on his tractor and asked how he's supposed to get hay to his cows on the far side of it, over","Warden Main","What did you tell him, over?","Sapper-6","Told him I didn't know, he watched us for an hour - then he went and cut his own fence so the cows could walk around to his side, over","Warden Main","Roger - move to the Echo Creek road, next berm in by dark, over","Sapper-6","Moving - be advised, the cows found the berm before the farmer did - six of them are standing on top of it like they own the county, over","Warden Main","Sapper-6, get the cows off my berm - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r2_d1_choir_riverside","military",1,3,10,20,1,{"Thoroughbred 2-6","Hatchet-6, Thoroughbred 2-6, civilians keep waving down my trucks, they say forty people are shut in a Baptist church in Riverside with those things all around it, over","Hatchet-6","Riverside is outside your sector - hold your road, over","Thoroughbred 2-6","Sir, one of my squad leaders has a wife who sings in that choir, over","Hatchet-6","I understand - hold your road - do you understand me, over?","Thoroughbred 2-6","I understand the order, over","Hatchet-6","Thoroughbred 2-6, count your men at 1800 and send me the number - Hatchet-6, out"}},
{"r2_mis_fire_channel_fuel","military_mistake",1,3,0,23,2,{"Striker-12","Foxtrot-11, Foxtrot-11, this is Striker-12 - where is the fuel truck, over?","Knox Dispatch","Unit calling on county fire, this is Knox County dispatch - I don't have a Foxtrot anything - identify yourself","Striker-12","Dispatch, this is Striker-12, United States Army - is Foxtrot-11 on this frequency, over?","Knox Dispatch","Son, the only trucks on this frequency are pumper trucks, and I'm down to two of those","Striker-7","Striker-12, Striker-7, you are on the civilian band - switch to your assigned net - out","Striker-12","Switching - sorry, ma'am - Striker-12, out","Knox Dispatch","Anytime, Army, if you find that fuel truck, we'd take a little too"}},
{"r2_mis_pound_cake_rate","military_mistake",1,7,11,20,1,{"Ruiz","I'll give you the pound cake and the cheese spread for your peanut butter and the matches","Tolliver","Cheese spread is not money, nobody wants cheese spread, it's a punishment in a little envelope","Ruiz","Fine, pound cake, cheese spread, and I take your guard shift at two","Tolliver","Now we're talking - throw in the hot sauce and it's a deal","Anvil-2-6","Station with the stuck handset, this is Anvil-2-6, the whole battalion now knows the exchange rate for pound cake - Unkey, over","Ruiz","Oh, no","Tolliver","Is it still on? Ruiz, is it still on?","Anvil-2-7","It is still on, Tolliver, and you are both pulling the two o'clock shift - together"}},
{"r2_mis_henry_ocean","military_mistake",1,4,0,23,1,{"Thoroughbred 2-3","Hatchet-6, Thoroughbred 2-3, road name follows - I spell - Henry, Ocean, Lincoln, Lincoln, Ocean, William - Hollow Road, over","Hatchet-6","Thoroughbred 2-3, Hatchet-6, that's the police alphabet - use the phonetic alphabet on this net, over","Thoroughbred 2-3","Sir, I've been a deputy for nineteen years and a Guardsman for six - Henry is how my mouth spells H, over","Hatchet-6","Hotel - say it with me - Hotel, over","Thoroughbred 2-3","Hotel, Oscar, Lima, Lima, Oscar, Whiskey - there - now can somebody come look at the six of them in the ditch on it, over?","Hatchet-6","Negative, you handle it, good spelling, Thoroughbred - Hatchet-6, out"}},
{"r2_mis_kyle_and_dwayne","military_mistake",1,5,0,23,1,{"Anvil-1-2","Dwayne, it's Kyle - you got the extra batteries in your truck, or did Hollister take them, over?","Anvil-1-7","Station using first names, this is Anvil-1-7, on this net we use callsigns, over","Anvil-1-2","Sorry, Sergeant - Anvil-1-3, this is Anvil-1-2 - you got the batteries, over?","Anvil-1-3","Anvil-1-2, Anvil-1-3, negative, Kyle, Hollister took them, over","Anvil-1-7","Anvil-1-3, what did I just say about first names?","Anvil-1-3","You said on the net, Sergeant, I was answering Kyle, over","Anvil-1-7","Both of you, my truck, right now - bring Hollister - bring the batteries - out"}},
{"r2_mis_welcome_to_muldraugh_twice","military_mistake",1,5,6,21,1,{"Mule-2","Warden Main, Mule-2, we are lost, over","Warden Main","Mule-2, send your grid, over","Mule-2","I don't have a military map of this county, I have a road atlas from a gas station - we are on page forty-one, over","Warden Main","Mule-2, what was the last sign you passed, over?","Mule-2","Welcome to Muldraugh, then another sign that said Welcome to Muldraugh, we're fairly sure it was the same sign, over","Warden Main","Mule-2, you're driving a loop around the town, at the next light, turn north onto the Dixie Highway, over","Mule-2","Roger, none of the lights are working - which way is north, over?","Warden Main","Toward the river, if you can see the river, you went too far - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r2_mis_pallet_of_blanks","military_mistake",1,4,0,23,1,{"Crowbar-7","Warden Main, Crowbar-7 - resupply received - be advised, the pallet is ten thousand rounds of blank ammunition, over","Warden Main","Say again, blank, over?","Crowbar-7","Blank, training rounds, the crimped kind, somebody grabbed the wrong pallet at the ammo point, over","Warden Main","Roger, send it back with the truck, over","Crowbar-7","Negative, the truck already left, the driver said good luck, and he meant it, over","Warden Main","Understood, live resupply tomorrow - what can you do with blanks, over?","Crowbar-7","Make noise, tonight I send two men to the far end of the soybean field with a rifle full of blanks and pull the dead off my wire, over","Warden Main","Approved, make sure those two men carry live rounds for the walk back - Warden Main, out"}},
{"r7_mil_freight_route_request","military",1,2,5,11,2,{"Freight-1-1","Roadmaster-3, this is Freight-1-1, request a route, over","Roadmaster-3","Freight-1-1, send your march unit, over","Freight-1-1","Eleven vehicles, four five-tons, two water trailers, two wreckers, three Humvees - start point is the armory at Elizabethtown, release point is the gate at Muldraugh, over","Roadmaster-3","Freight-1-1, take US-31W the whole way, do not use the interstate, speed forty, interval fifty meters, halt at the top of each hour, over","Freight-1-1","Roger - is 31W trafficable both lanes, over?","Roadmaster-3","Both lanes to the Salt River bridge, after the bridge the northbound is stacked with civilian vehicles and you will be in one lane, over","Freight-1-1","Understood one lane - Roadmaster-3, who has the road at the bridge, over?","Roadmaster-3","Kentucky State Police at the south end and one of ours at the north - neither of them knows you're coming, I'm telling them now, over","Freight-1-1","Freight-1-1 rolling at {time} - Roadmaster-3, Freight-1-1, out"}},
{"r7_mil_freight_bridge_class","military",1,3,6,14,1,{"Freight-1-1","Roadmaster-3, Freight-1-1, I've picked up a lowboy with a dozer on it - what's the bridge class on your route, over?","Roadmaster-3","Freight-1-1, say the weight of that load, over","Freight-1-1","Tractor, trailer, dozer - call it eighty thousand pounds. Nothing heavier on this road today, over","Roadmaster-3","Stand by. County map hasn't got bridge classes, and my state map's from 1987, over","Freight-1-1","Waiting","Roadmaster-3","Freight-1-1, the 31W bridges will carry it, the county road bridges will not, and two of them have got a wood deck - stay on 31W, over","Freight-1-1","Roger, 31W only - Roadmaster-3, if somebody puts a roadblock across 31W, what's my detour, over?","Roadmaster-3","No detour that'll take that weight. You'll have to wait for them to clear 31W, over","Freight-1-1","Freight-1-1 copies. Stay on 31W, and wait if it's blocked. Out"}},
{"r7_mil_wrong_net_medevac","military_mistake",1,3,0,23,1,{"Cardinal-2-4","Any station this net, Cardinal-2-4, I need to know when our chow truck's coming, over","Dustoff Operations","Station calling, this is Dustoff Operations, you're on the medevac net, over","Cardinal-2-4","Say again, over?","Dustoff Operations","You're on the medical evacuation net, this frequency is for nine line requests only - get off it, over","Cardinal-2-4","Roger, sorry - Dustoff Operations, which one is the one I'm supposed to be on, over?","Dustoff Operations","I don't have your unit's frequencies, son - go find your platoon sergeant and look at the card in his pocket, over","Cardinal-2-4","He's asleep sat up in a truck and I've been told twice not to wake him, over","Dustoff Operations","Then wake him for this - tell him a helicopter crew told you to - Dustoff Operations, out"}},
{"r7_mil_freq_change_execute","military",1,3,5,21,2,{"Cardinal Main","All Cardinal stations, this is Cardinal Main - frequency change - go to the alternate at {time}, acknowledge in order, over","Cardinal-1-6","Cardinal-1-6, roger alternate at {time}, over","Cardinal-2-6","Cardinal-2-6, roger, over","Cardinal-3-6","Cardinal-3-6, roger - Main, I've got two sets that won't hold the alternate - their knobs are worn loose, over","Cardinal Main","Cardinal-3-6, tape the knob, masking tape, a wrap of it, right over the dial, over","Cardinal-3-6","Roger tape - Main, that's genuinely the fix, over?","Cardinal Main","That's genuinely the fix, it has been the fix since Korea, see you on the alternate - Cardinal Main, out"}},
{"r7_mil_boone_main_state_call","military",1,2,6,12,2,{"Boone Main","All stations, this is Boone Main, net call for the state - report in order of armory number and keep it to one sentence, over","Armory 21","Armory 21, Elizabethtown, sixty-one present, one company committed south of the river, over","Boone Main","Armory 21, roger - next, over","Armory 21","Boone Main, I'm the only one answering, I've been listening to this net since five and I'm the only station that's come up, over","Boone Main","Armory 21, stand by","Boone Main","All stations, this is Boone Main, if you hear this and cannot reach me, send a vehicle to the nearest armory that can - do not wait for us to call you, over","Armory 21","Boone Main, Armory 21 - what do I do with sixty-one soldiers and no orders, over?","Boone Main","You go to Knox County and you help, that's the order and it's the only one I have the authority to give you this morning - Boone Main, out"}},
{"r7_mil_no_maps_of_the_county","military_mistake",1,3,6,23,1,{"Cardinal-2-6","Cardinal Main, 2-6, I need map sheets for this county - I've got two and they're both of the wrong end of it, over","Cardinal Main","2-6, there are no more map sheets, what came in the bag is what there is, over","Cardinal-2-6","Main, I'm moving a platoon on a gas station road map one of my sergeants paid for himself, over","Cardinal Main","Then that's your map. 2-6, mark it up and don't lose it, over","Cardinal-2-6","Roger - Main, the road map has got county roads on it that the military sheet doesn't, so honestly it's the better map, over","Cardinal Main","2-6, write that in your log and put the sergeant's name on it - somebody ought to owe him four dollars someday, over","Cardinal-2-6","It was three ninety-nine and he mentions it hourly. 2-6, out"}},
{"r7_nights_truck_keys_in_it","scanner",1,2,1,5,1,{"Dispatch","All Knox units, be on the lookout for a red Ford pickup, Kentucky plate, taken out of the Sav Rite lot about an hour ago","Dispatch","Owner left it running with the keys in it while he went in - he'd like it back and he'd like us not to mention it to his wife","Knox 26","Knox 26, dispatch, I got a red Ford sitting crossways in Halbert Street with both doors standing open","Dispatch","Knox 26, is it running?","Knox 26","Still running - radio's on, nobody in it, nobody around it, and there's a grocery sack in the seat with the ice cream melted through the bottom","Dispatch","Any damage to it?","Knox 26","Front bumper's got hair on it, it ain't deer hair","Dispatch","Say again your last, Knox 26?","Knox 26","I said I'm sitting right here with my lights on till Kidwell gets to me - then we'll both look at the bumper"}},
{"r7_nights_jail_wont_take_him","scanner",1,2,23,4,1,{"Knox 24","Jail Desk, Knox 24, I'm coming to you with one male, assault, and he's got a bite on his forearm the victim put there","Jail Desk","Knox 24, negative, sheriff's standing order come down this afternoon - we don't book nobody with a bite till a doctor clears them","Knox 24","Which doctor? The hospital's got people laid on the floor in the hallway","Jail Desk","I know it, that's the order, 24, I'm reading it off the paper taped on the wall right here","Knox 24","So where's he go?","Jail Desk","Wait one","Jail Desk","Knox 24, the jailer says the answer is he stays with you","Knox 24","He stays with me, in my car, behind my head - all night","Jail Desk","That's what the man said, jail Desk out"}},
{"r7_nights_back_seat_three_hours","scanner",1,3,1,6,2,{"Knox 24","Knox 20, Knox 24, that's three hours I've had this fella in the back seat - he quit talking about an hour ago","Knox 20","Quit talking how?","Knox 24","Quit talking like a man that's done arguing, he's just sat there with his head against the cage looking at the back of my neck","Knox 20","Is he breathing?","Knox 24","Yeah, hard - Sarge, his arm's gone black up past the elbow","Knox 20","Pull in at the fire hall on 31W, leave him in the car, get out, and stand where I can see you when I come up the road","Knox 24","Copy - Knox 20, he asked me for a drink of water when we left the Legion and I told him in a minute - I never did give it to him","Knox 20","We'll get him one - stand outside the car, 24"}},
{"r7_nights_shots_dry_creek","scanner",1,3,22,3,2,{"Dispatch","Knox 22, shots fired, 2205 Dry Creek Road, neighbor says the man across the road is shooting into his own front yard","Knox 22","Knox 22 en route - any idea what he's shooting at?","Dispatch","He hollered at the neighbor that he's shooting his brother-in-law - caller says the brother-in-law's been dead since Tuesday","Knox 22","Say again, dispatch?","Dispatch","Since Tuesday, 22, that's what she told me and she said it twice without me asking","Knox 22","Knox 22 is 10-23 and I'm staying behind my door - he's reloading on the porch, I got a light on him and he ain't once looked up","Knox 22","Dispatch, there's a man out in that yard walking at the porch - he's been shot, he is walking at the porch","Dispatch","Knox 22, say again, is your subject hit?","Knox 22","The man in the yard's hit, four, five times, he's still coming, I'm getting my rifle out of the trunk"}},
{"r7_nights_reserve_no_vest","scanner",1,3,20,23,1,{"Knox 20","Knox 18, Knox 20 - you in a car yet?","Knox 18","Knox 18, yes sir, Unit 16 - Sarge, this car's got no shotgun and the vest in the trunk says extra large and I ain't","Knox 20","Wear it anyhow, wear it loose and keep your sleeves down - how long since you rode a reserve shift?","Knox 18","Since the fair - last September","Knox 20","Then you ride with Kidwell tonight, you do what he says when he says it, and you don't get out of the car first - not one time","Knox 18","Yes sir - Knox 20, my wife wants to know when I'm off","Knox 20","Tell her I'll let the both of you know together - Knox 20 out"}},
{"r7_nights_county_line_bicycle","scanner",1,3,22,3,2,{"Dispatch","Knox 22, Hardin County's asking help at 6600 Salt River Road - it sits right on the line and their car is forty minutes out","Knox 22","Knox 22, that's four minutes from me - what's the call?","Dispatch","Domestic, wife's locked in the bathroom, she says her husband bit their boy and the boy went out the front door","Knox 22","How old's the boy?","Dispatch","Eleven - Hardin says he took off up the road on a bicycle","Knox 22","Find the boy before the house - tell everybody, ours and theirs - eleven years old, bicycle, Salt River Road","Dispatch","It's going out right now","Knox 22","Bicycle, dispatch - tell 'em to look in the ditches for a bicycle"}},
{"r7_nights_woman_on_31w","scanner",1,3,2,5,1,{"Dispatch","Knox 26, truck driver reports a woman walking south on 31W near the weigh station - says she's in a nightgown and won't get off the road","Knox 26","Knox 26 en route - did he stop for her?","Dispatch","He slowed and hollered and she never turned her head - he called it in off the payphone at the truck stop","Knox 26","Knox 26, I'm on her, she's walking the white line southbound","Dispatch","Knox 26, do you need EMS?","Knox 26","Dispatch, stand by one, I'm getting out","Knox 26","Dispatch, she's fine, seventy-some years old, barefoot, and she says she's walking to West Point to see about her sister","Knox 26","I told her I'd drive her, she said she'd rather walk, and then she got in - show me 10-8 toward West Point"}},
{"r7_nights_child_put_the_gate_up","scanner",1,2,0,4,2,{"Dispatch","Knox 22, I got a child on the phone from 415 Wickham Street - she says her daddy's acting funny and he's locked in the bathroom","Knox 22","Knox 22 en route - how old is she?","Dispatch","Seven or eight, her name's Ada, she's calm as anything, 22, she give me the street number twice without me asking","Knox 22","Anybody else in the house?","Dispatch","A baby, she says the baby's asleep in the playpen and she put the gate up at the end of the hall","Knox 22","She put the gate up","Dispatch","She put the gate up, I'm keeping her on the line till you knock","Knox 22","Knock's coming - tell her a deputy named Roy is on the porch and he's got a flashlight, so don't be scared of the light"}},
{"r7_ksp_post4_three_cars_down","scanner",1,2,6,10,2,{"Post 4","Post 4 to all units on the day shift, before anybody asks, we have three cars down in the garage and no parts coming from Frankfort","Trooper 406","Post 4, 406 - do I get a car or do I ride with somebody?","Post 4","406, you have 418's car when he comes in at two - until then you're at the post answering the phone","Trooper 406","406 copies - how many calls are holding for the parkway?","Post 4","Twenty-six on the parkways and eleven on 31W, most of them are abandoned vehicles and I'm not sending anybody to those","Trooper 418","Post 4, 418, I'm still on the parkway at milepost 94 and my low fuel light's been on since Radcliff","Post 4","418, the pumps at the post are working - come in, fill up, and hand that car to 406 at the door"}},
{"r7_ksp_wkp_94_no_wrecker","scanner",1,3,7,19,1,{"Trooper 418","Post 4, 418, I'm 10-23 on a 10-50 westbound on the Western Kentucky Parkway, milepost 94 - two vehicles, both in the median","Post 4","418, injuries?","Trooper 418","One driver's up and walking and cussing me, the other car's empty and the driver's door is off the hinges","Post 4","Empty how?","Trooper 418","Empty like whoever was in it got out and walked off - there's a diaper bag in the back and a shoe on the shoulder - no blood in the seat","Post 4","Copy, I'll try for a wrecker out of Leitchfield - last two I called won't roll on the parkway after noon","Trooper 418","Then have the road department push both of these off the pavement and I'll sit here till they come","Post 4","418, the road department has one truck and it's on 31W - you may be sitting a while"}},
{"r7_ksp_bluegrass_people_walking","scanner",1,2,9,20,2,{"Trooper 422","Post 4, 422, traffic is stopped dead eastbound on the Bluegrass Parkway from the Bardstown exit back about two miles","Post 4","422, what's the holdup?","Trooper 422","Nothing's wrong with the road, they're stopped because people are out of their cars walking up the shoulder to ask somebody what's going on","Post 4","Who are they asking?","Trooper 422","Each other, post 4, I've got maybe forty people on foot between the lanes and a dog loose in all of it","Post 4","Get them back in their vehicles and moving, radio says Louisville's closed the interstate at the county line","Trooper 422","Then where am I sending them, Post 4? East is where they were going","Post 4","Send them back west and let Post 3 have the argument - that's all I've got for you, 422"}},
{"r7_ksp_escort_church_bus","scanner",1,3,8,18,1,{"Post 4","Trooper 406, we have a request for an escort, church bus out of Rosewood, thirty-one aboard, wanting to get to Bardstown","Trooper 406","406, I'll take it - where do I meet them?","Post 4","The Amoco at the parkway ramp, driver's name is Hollis and he says the bus won't do better than fifty-five","Trooper 406","Fifty-five's fine - post 4, is Bardstown taking people?","Post 4","Nelson County says their armory is full and their high school is full - that's the last I heard and that was this morning","Trooper 406","Do you want me to tell the driver that before we roll or after?","Post 4","Before, he's carrying thirty-one people and he's entitled to decide with the truth in front of him","Trooper 406","Copy, I'll tell him and we'll go anyway - that's what he's gonna say, I already know what he's gonna say"}},
{"r7_trans_fourteen_to_lagrange","scanner",1,2,6,11,2,{"Jail Desk","Knox 3, Jail Desk, the transport's loaded, fourteen going to the state facility at LaGrange, two deputies on the bus","Knox 3","Jail Desk, has LaGrange confirmed they'll take fourteen?","Jail Desk","They confirmed yesterday at four, I ain't got them back on the phone since","Knox 3","Then confirm again before that bus pulls out of the port","Jail Desk","Knox 3, I have called that number nine times this morning - it rings and rings","Knox 3","Nine times","Jail Desk","Nine - Knox 3, we've got twenty-two men in a jail built for sixteen and I've got a bus running in the port","Knox 3","Roll the bus - take the route through Shepherdsville and call me from a payphone at Bullitt County"}},
{"r7_trans_bus_at_the_port","scanner",1,2,7,12,1,{"Transport 1","Jail Desk, Transport 1, we're out of the sally port with fourteen - count is fourteen, chains are on, and we're rolling at {time}","Jail Desk","Transport 1, copy fourteen at {time} - what's your route?","Transport 1","31W to Shepherdsville, then north - Knox 3 said no interstate and no Louisville","Jail Desk","Copy - Transport 1, one of them wants me to call his mother and tell her where he's going","Transport 1","Which one of them?","Jail Desk","The Cobb boy - Junior","Transport 1","Call her, tell her he's fine and tell her he asked about her first thing - he did, too"}},
{"r7_trans_state_wont_take_them","scanner",1,2,9,15,2,{"Transport 1","Jail Desk, Transport 1, we're stopped at a payphone at Bullitt County, I got through to LaGrange","Jail Desk","Go ahead, Transport 1","Transport 1","They're not taking anybody, not fourteen, not one, they're not opening that gate for a county bus today or any day this week","Jail Desk","Did he give you a reason?","Transport 1","The man said they've got their own problem inside and he said it in a voice I didn't care for - then he hung up on me","Jail Desk","Stand by, I'll get Knox 3","Transport 1","Jail Desk, I'm parked at a gas station on a state highway with fourteen chained men and two deputies - don't take long"}},
{"r7_trans_one_coughing_in_back","scanner",1,2,10,16,1,{"Transport 1","Jail Desk, Transport 1, we've got a man in the back row coughing and he's hot to the touch","Jail Desk","Which one?","Transport 1","Second from the window, he was fine at the port, he signed his own property sheet, and now he can't hold his head up","Jail Desk","Is he chained to somebody?","Transport 1","He's chained to two men and they've both figured out what I'm asking you - it's gotten real quiet on this bus","Jail Desk","Transport 1, hold on, I'm going to the jailer","Transport 1","I don't have a hold on in me, Jail Desk - tell me to take the chain off him or tell me not to - say it on the radio so it's said","Jail Desk","Take it off him and move him to the front - that's from the jailer's mouth and I'm writing the time down"}},
{"r7_trans_stopped_at_checkpoint","scanner",1,3,10,18,2,{"Transport 1","Jail Desk, Transport 1, we're stopped at an Army checkpoint on 31W and they will not let this bus through","Jail Desk","Transport 1, did you show them the transport order?","Transport 1","I showed him everything in the folder, he's nineteen years old and he's real polite and he keeps saying he don't have anything about a bus","Jail Desk","Can he call somebody?","Transport 1","He did, he came back and said his sergeant says no county buses north, period, and then he apologized to me twice","Jail Desk","So you're turning around","Transport 1","I'm turning around, jail Desk, that boy asked me if the men on the bus had had anything to eat - he's holding a rifle and that's what he asked me"}},
{"r7_trans_shackle_key_argument","scanner",1,3,11,19,1,{"Transport 1","Jail Desk, Transport 1, whoever loaded this bus sent us out with one shackle key and it's the wrong one","Jail Desk","Wrong how?","Transport 1","That key does the belly chains, not the leg irons - bus catches fire, fourteen men burn in their seats","Jail Desk","Transport 1, there's a spare in the property room","Transport 1","That's forty minutes behind me, jail Desk, I want it on the radio that I said this out loud before it mattered","Jail Desk","It's said and it's logged at {time}, I put your words in quotes","Transport 1","Good, now send somebody with the key and I'll sit on the shoulder and count heads till he gets here"}},
{"r7_trans_turned_back_at_the_line","scanner",1,3,13,20,1,{"Knox 3","Transport 1, Knox 3 - bring them home","Transport 1","Knox 3, home is a jail built for sixteen with twenty-two in it already","Knox 3","I know what it is, there's nowhere else in this state that will open a door for us today","Transport 1","What do I tell them? They're sat back there listening to every word, Knox 3 - they know the road's the wrong direction","Knox 3","Tell them the truth, tell them LaGrange said no and the county's got them back","Transport 1","One of them just asked me if that's good news or bad news","Knox 3","And what did you say back to him?","Transport 1","I told him I didn't know, he said he'd take it either way as long as somebody quits chaining him to a sick man"}},
{"r7_ems_more_than_we_can_carry","scanner",1,2,22,4,2,{"EMS 1","Dispatch, EMS 1 on scene at the Legion hall, I've got more patients than I've got hands, start me everything in the county","Dispatch","EMS 1, how many patients?","EMS 1","Seven that I can see, three are bad - one of them's got an arterial bleed at the neck and the deputies are holding pressure with bar towels","Dispatch","EMS 1, I have Medic 2 out of service and Medic 3 forty minutes out","EMS 1","Then I'm taking the neck and one more and the rest go by private vehicle - tell the hospital I'm coming with two and I'll be hot","Dispatch","Copy two - EMS 1, who decides which ones go in the cars?","EMS 1","I do - right now, dispatch, put the time in the log, {time}, and put my name by it"}},
{"r7_ems_hospital_on_divert","scanner",1,3,0,23,1,{"Hospital","All EMS units, Knox County Hospital, we are closed to everything - trauma, medical, all of it, do not bring us patients","Medic 3","Hospital, Medic 3, I'm three minutes from your door with a fifty year old man in respiratory distress","Hospital","Medic 3, we have fourteen in a hallway built for four and we have no doctor in the building right now","Medic 3","Say again, no doctor?","Hospital","Doctor Freeman's been on since Friday and he's asleep in the chapel - I'm not waking him for the eleventh time in two hours","Medic 3","Hospital, where do I go?","Hospital","Hardin Memorial's on divert too - Medic 3, bring him - bring him and put him in the hallway and I'll find you a spot on the floor","Medic 3","Copy - Medic 3 coming in, and when I get there I'm bringing my own cot back out with me"}},
{"r7_school_open_the_gym","scanner",1,1,8,16,2,{"Base","Base to all buses, the board voted this morning and we're opening Muldraugh Elementary as a shelter starting at noon","Bus 12","Bus 12, Base - you want us hauling people to it?","Base","That's exactly it, bus 12, you run the trailer park on the bypass - bus 7, you run Halbert Street and the apartments","Bus 7","Bus 7 copies - base, how many trips?","Base","Until the gym's full or until you run out of daylight, and I'd rather it be the daylight","Bus 12","Base, do we take dogs?","Base","Wait one, Bus 12","Base","Bus 12, the principal says no dogs in the gym - she also says she ain't going to be standing at the door checking, so do what you think is right"}},
}
